    },
    {
      "requested_feature": "Iterative tuning of the Software and Travel programs after go-live.",
      "reason_unsupported": "Spend programs support GET and POST only; there is no PATCH or DELETE, so a program is effectively immutable once created via the API. This raises the stakes on reviewing the two programs before they are created.",
      "evidence": "openapi snapshot 2026_08_30 — /spend-programs has GET and POST only and /spend-programs/{id} is GET-only; there is no PATCH or DELETE, so programs are immutable via the API.",
      "proposed_manual_workaround": "Get programs right the first time, or edit in-app. This raises the stakes on the config review before go-live and is worth saying in the handoff."
    },
    {
      "requested_feature": "Distinct permission levels for a CEO, a VP Finance, a Controller, an office manager, an IT administrator and an external contractor.",
      "reason_unsupported": "Acme's six distinct roles must be mapped onto Ramp's six fixed roles, which carry no seniority or scoping dimension. Each non-obvious mapping is recorded individually in assumptions_made.",
      "evidence": "openapi snapshot 2026_08_30 plus support.ramp.com 'User roles overview', checked 2026-08-30 — Ramp exposes six assignable roles with fixed, documented permission sets and no seniority or scoping dimension, so mapping customer titles onto them is a per-person judgement call.",
      "proposed_manual_workaround": "Every non-obvious mapping gets an assumptions_made entry naming the title, the chosen role, and what the person will consequently be able to see or do. Bookkeeper for close-the-books staff, AUDITOR for read-only compliance, GUEST_USER for contractors (see CAP-GUEST-EXPIRY-DEFAULT), IT_ADMIN for identity owners (see CAP-IT-ADMIN-SCOPE), BUSINESS_ADMIN for owners (see DRIFT-ROLE-BUSINESS-OWNER). Never infer a role from seniority alone."
    }
  ]
}

